the company's own revenue, profit, cash or credit risk, judged against the company's size as the item states it, not only against a total of its kind or another deal. Write no figure the item does not give; this field is reasoning, not evidence. When the item gives no measure of the company's size or no amount for the obligation itself, say so and judge qualitatively from what it does state: whom the obligation backs, for what and for how long (the cost of a project or asset is not the obligation's amount). For any other opens_as, null.\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c11-schema.json:67:     \"settled_by\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c11-schema.json:72:     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c11-schema.json:83:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1-schema.json:20:     \"closest_open_thesis\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1-schema.json:21:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1-schema.json:47:     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1-schema.json:58:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c9-system.txt:126:- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c12-closing.txt:15:For each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c7-closing.txt:15:For each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it unlinked.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle-matters.md:13:2. A matter both readers list is kept (`settled_by: both`). Keep the better quote; it must be an exact span of the article.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle-matters.md:15:   keep it (`settled_by: third`) or drop it, with one short reason.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle-matters.md:22:                                \"quote\": \"<exact span>\", \"strength\": \"core|supporting\", \"settled_by\": \"both|third\", \"reason\": \"...\"}]},\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:20:     \"opens_as\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:21:     \"settled_by\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:22:     \"closest_open_thesis\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:23:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:49:     \"opens_as\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:59:     \"settled_by\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:64:     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:75:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c5-schema.json:20:     \"closest_open_thesis\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
